{"id": "EUVD-2026-103616", "enisaUuid": "f25dab8b-8b43-3c88-89fa-3574840a4b28", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: stmmac: clear stale buf->page after recycling on skb build failure\n\nIn stmmac_rx(), when napi_build_skb() fails the descriptor page is\nrecycled back to the page pool with page_pool_recycle_direct(), but\nbuf->page is left pointing at the recycled page, unlike every other\nconsumption site in the function which clears the pointer after handing\nthe page away.\n\nWith the stale pointer stmmac_rx_refill() skips the replacement\nallocation and programs the already-recycled page back into the RX\ndescriptor.\n\nClear buf->page on the napi_build_skb() failure path to keep the buffer\nlifecycle consistent with the other consumption sites.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:37", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/501baaeca7d128fa0a2f6953cf5873c5b0d7cf89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/298673397ea3f6f5811b84f0d9f71eac71dda2e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0a7822e34a0bfde31b194ac3da3253e5032b44cc"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98571", "GHSA-j482-jx6v-w2pf"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "250561a9-1493-3e50-9ffe-5cce73130dca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df542f669307918f054a17878ff6dd1ddbb2fe18 <0a7822e34a0bfde31b194ac3da3253e5032b44cc"}, {"id": "2d62eb48-7991-3c4d-8497-ecbf9b3c05d9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df542f669307918f054a17878ff6dd1ddbb2fe18 <298673397ea3f6f5811b84f0d9f71eac71dda2e3"}, {"id": "49d07354-7ae7-3821-ba39-d65710bb6df9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "59d180a0-0b43-316d-86ef-de58a77539ce", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14"}, {"id": "7cf374b5-8ea8-3156-ae1b-8cb286469132", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "df542f669307918f054a17878ff6dd1ddbb2fe18 <501baaeca7d128fa0a2f6953cf5873c5b0d7cf89"}, {"id": "9cc5ab92-0db7-38f2-8bff-4737f6424388", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "b4463c4c-c690-3669-be5e-afb4c2999053", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "e8031df0-118b-38ba-bcf6-4a68dc8a334c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b1a97608-1697-329c-ab9f-2508c617bd96", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}